From: iLinux workspace
Subject: [PATCH] proxy, server: AF_UNIX stream sockets on macOS

macOS rejects socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_SEQPACKET) with EPROTONOSUPPORT, so
the Venus proxy could not start ("failed to create socket pair: Protocol not
supported").  The macOS patch set already frames messages with a length
header on non-seqpacket sockets; create SOCK_STREAM pairs there.

diff -ru a/server/render_socket.c b/server/render_socket.c
--- a/server/render_socket.c	2026-10-12 11:42:41
+++ b/server/render_socket.c	2026-10-12 11:42:41
@@ -53,7 +53,9 @@
 render_socket_pair(int out_fds[static 2])
 {
 #ifdef __APPLE__
-   int type = SOCK_SEQPACKET;
+   /* macOS has no AF_UNIX SOCK_SEQPACKET: use a stream; messages are then
+    * framed with a length header (see the !is_seqpacket paths). */
+   int type = SOCK_STREAM;
 #else
    int type = SOCK_SEQPACKET;
 #endif
diff -ru a/src/proxy/proxy_socket.c b/src/proxy/proxy_socket.c
--- a/src/proxy/proxy_socket.c	2026-10-12 11:42:41
+++ b/src/proxy/proxy_socket.c	2026-10-12 11:42:41
@@ -43,7 +43,9 @@
 proxy_socket_pair(int out_fds[static 2])
 {
 #ifdef __APPLE__
-   int type = SOCK_SEQPACKET;
+   /* macOS has no AF_UNIX SOCK_SEQPACKET: use a stream; messages are then
+    * framed with a length header (see the !is_seqpacket paths). */
+   int type = SOCK_STREAM;
 #else
    int type = SOCK_SEQPACKET;
 #endif
